{
  "id": "u02-l04b",
  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "Is not: নই, নও, নন, নয়",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "'Is' has no word in Bengali, but **'is not'** does, and it changes with the person, just like আছি / আছো / আছেন:\n\n- আমি ছাত্র **নই** (*noi*): I'm not a student\n- তুমি ছাত্র **নও** (*noo*, said *no-o*): you're not\n- আপনি / উনি ছাত্র **নন** (*non*): you / he (polite) aren't\n- সে / ও ছাত্র **নয়** (*noy*): he / she isn't (also এটা … নয়: it isn't)\n\n**নয় or নেই?** নয় (and নই / নও / নন) denies *what* someone is: রাফি ডাক্তার **নয়**. **নেই** denies that someone is *there*: রাফি এখানে **নেই**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "noi",
      "bn": "নই",
      "tr": "noi",
      "en": "am not",
      "notes": "Goes with আমি / আমরা: আমি ছাত্র নই."
    },
    {
      "id": "noo",
      "bn": "নও",
      "tr": "noo",
      "en": "are not (familiar)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুমি / তোমরা."
    },
    {
      "id": "non",
      "bn": "নন",
      "tr": "non",
      "en": "is not / are not (polite)",
      "notes": "Goes with আপনি, তিনি, উনি."
    },
    {
      "id": "noy-isnt",
      "bn": "নয়",
      "tr": "noy",
      "en": "is not",
      "notes": "Goes with সে, ও, এটা. In everyday Bangladeshi speech না is used for all persons: আমি ছাত্র না. নয় is also the number nine (Unit 5)."
    }
  ],
